    changelogEntry136: "Multi-club support: members of more than one club now see a club switcher in the header to toggle between clubs; users in a single club see no change.",
    changelog_2026_06_04: "June 4, 2026",
    changelogEntry137: "Athletes can now open the Injury Rehab plan again from the side menu.",
    changelogEntry138: "Coaches can now request a post-competition evaluation directly from the athlete view.",
    changelogEntry139: "New tool in the Library: check supplements and medicine against anti-doping knowledge based on WADA's list.",
    changelog_2026_06_06: "June 6, 2026",
    changelog_2026_06_05: "June 5, 2026",
    changelogEntry140: "Improved readability: text colors now follow the surface automatically, fixing white-on-light text on several screens.",
    changelogEntry141: "Coach navigation restructured: Today and Messages are now their own pages, and the coach dashboard focuses on the squad.",
    changelogEntry142: "Library reorganized: Exercises, Mental, Recipes, and HIIT now use the same category sections with icons and item counts as Physical Tests.",
    changelogEntry144: "Coach invite links now auto-approve: athletes who join via a coach's invite link get instant access — no admin approval required.",
    changelogEntry145: "Coach video uploads now enforce 1-video-per-athlete: uploading a new video prompts you to export the old video's notes as a PDF before it is replaced. Antidoping & supplement check is now free for all athletes (including solo subscribers); solo athletes also keep full competition + reflection access. Help center updated to reflect the new flows.",
    changelog_2026_06_25: "June 25, 2026",
    changelogEntry155: "Onboarding fixes: unselected option buttons (discipline, goals, coach focus) now have proper contrast in dark mode, and save errors on the final step show a specific message (e.g. 'Age must be between 5 and 99') instead of a generic one — expired sessions also auto-recover.",
    changelog_2026_06_26: "June 26, 2026",
    changelog_2026_06_27: "June 27, 2026",
    changelog_2026_07_02: "July 2, 2026",
    changelogEntry157: "Nutrition: meal categories (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner, Snacks) are now collapsible.",
    changelogEntry158: "Fix: improved text contrast in Exercise 'Key Form Cues' and similar light surface cards across the app.",
    changelogEntry156: "Fix: members of clubs with an active license now have access to all modules without a personal subscription.",
    changelog_2026_06_23: "June 23, 2026",
    changelogEntry152: "Coach Mental Review rebuilt: the 6 categories now mirror the athlete's 6 mental dimensions from a coaching perspective (composure under pressure, sideline calm, decisions under chaos, role model after a loss, coach confidence, motivation & burnout). Spanish (es) is now fully supported in this feature.",
    changelogEntry153: "Coach Mental Review expanded: each of the 6 categories now has 5 questions (30 total, up from 18) for a deeper monthly snapshot of your inner coaching game. Total score still out of 30.",
    changelogEntry154: "New Taekwondo Drills library — a curated, shared catalog of drills with video links, organised by category (kicks, combinations, footwork, poomsae, sparring, conditioning). Global drills set by the platform admin are visible to every club; club-specific drills stay inside your club.",
    changelog_2026_06_17: "June 17, 2026",
    changelogEntry151: "Physical testing is now the main library page — no more modal. Open Library → Testing and you land directly on the tabbed view with Start test / Results, Progression and Compare athletes.",
    changelogEntry150: "Test catalog is now collapsed by category with distinct colored icons, so you can scan and pick a test much faster on mobile.",
    changelogEntry149: "Health is temporarily hidden from the menu until native HealthKit / Health Connect sync ships with the React Native app.",
    
    changelog_2026_06_12: "June 12, 2026",
    changelogEntry148: "Homepage refresh: founder credibility, side-by-side comparison vs. the status quo, role-split CTAs. Built by a coach, not a startup.",
    changelogEntry147: "Onboarding now has a 'Continue later' button. Your progress is saved locally and restored next time you sign in on the same device.",
    changelogEntry146: "Help center now opens as a full page (no more overlay), keeping you logged in and inside the app.",
